/* book: lead: Activity coefficients γ measure how far a liquid mixture is from ideal. Models for γ come from the excess Gibbs energy GE: differentiate GE and you get ln γ. The Margules, van Laar and Wilson equations are three such models with fitted constants. Engineers use them to predict non-ideal vapour-liquid equilibrium (VLE), distillation columns and azeotropes. Only a few universities teach this chapter  */
